::PC_U05_L03_Q01::
Question ID: PC_U05_L03_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.PC.VC.4
Question:
Which statement is correct about complex numbers in polar or trigonometric form?
{
~A. The modulus is always the real part only.#This choice misses the key structure of the lesson. Return to the definition and identify the required feature before choosing an answer.
=B. The modulus gives distance from the origin and the argument gives direction.#Correct. Polar and trigonometric forms use distance from the origin and angle direction.
~C. The argument is always the imaginary part only.#This choice misses the key structure of the lesson. Return to the definition and identify the required feature before choosing an answer.
~D. Trigonometric form removes the need for an angle.#This choice misses the key structure of the lesson. Return to the definition and identify the required feature before choosing an answer.
}
